A line of plain prose pasted among statements (no comment marker). The
apostrophe in "doesn't" opens a string literal that runs to end of file:
unterminated_string on the `'`, and nothing after the opener is checked.
The statement's parse already fails at the second word, before the
string, so unexpected_token still reports that token; it defers only
when the token it stops on is the unterminated string itself
(diag.unterminated_string second Flags fence, diag.unexpected_token).
-- input.ssl --
:DECLARE nCount;
nCount := 1;
This line was pasted from the ticket, but it doesn't belong here.
nCount := 2;
